<Base title="Privacy Policy | Neelkanth Mahadev Temple Guide" description="Privacy policy of the independent Neelkanth Mahadev Temple (Shree Neelkanth Mahadev Temple) visitor guide — cookies, Google Analytics and Google Maps." path="/en/privacy/" locale="en" alternates={alternates}>
<section class="section"><article class="container prose legal max-w-4xl"><p class="eyebrow">Legal</p><h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black">Privacy Policy</h1><p><strong>Last updated: 21 October 2026</strong></p><h2>What information we may collect</h2><p>We try to limit collection to the minimum information needed to run the service. This may include IP address, general technical details of browser/device, pages viewed, referrer information and usage data obtained from cookies/similar technologies. This site has no account, booking, payment or contact form.</p><h2>How we use information</h2><ul><li>To improve reliability, content and experience</li><li>To understand aggregate traffic and usage patterns</li><li>To meet applicable legal obligations</li></ul><h2>Google Analytics</h2><p>Google Analytics 4 may be used after consent for analytics cookies. We have set up GA to load on a consent basis. Withdrawing permission turns off Google Analytics on the current page. If browser storage fails, a status message shows the limit; on a new tab or refresh the earlier choice may be re-read. You can change Google Analytics consent in <a href="/en/cookies/">Cookie Settings</a>.</p><h2>Hosting and Cloudflare Web Analytics</h2><p>The hosting layer may independently add a Cloudflare Web Analytics script, collecting performance and timing measurements of page loads. This is a service separate from Google Analytics; rejecting Google Analytics in this site’s cookie settings does not turn off this hosting measurement. See Cloudflare’s <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/data-metrics/data-origin-and-collection/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">data collection details</a> and <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/faq/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FAQ</a>.</p><h2>Google Maps and external content</h2><p>The map page uses a Google Maps embed. Loading it may give Google some technical information including your IP address and browser data. Such services handle data under their own privacy policies and terms.</p><h2>Weather and offline</h2><p>The hosting server fetches the Open-Meteo forecast from the temple’s public coordinates; your private location is not requested. The hosting provider may process technical request details. A Service Worker may keep viewed pages and static content in your browser for offline use. Clearing browser site data may remove this cache and your analytics preference.</p><h2>Image source</h2><p>The historic temple photo is by Rahuldewangan (23 March 2010), released into the public domain on Wikimedia Commons. The shared card is made from it. Today’s view may differ; the source link is on the home page.</p><h2>Your rights</h2><p>Applicable data-protection laws, which may include rules like GDPR depending on circumstances, may give you rights such as access to, correction and deletion of your personal data, objection/restriction of processing, and complaint to a competent supervisory authority. Rights may differ by jurisdiction.</p><h2>Data retention</h2><p>We do not intend to keep personal data longer than necessary for the purpose and legal/security needs. Analytics retention periods may follow their configuration and policy.</p><h2>Children’s privacy</h2><p>This site is not designed to knowingly collect personal data from children.</p><h2>Policy changes</h2><p>This policy may be revised when technology or law changes. For important travel or legal decisions, see the latest version of this page.</p></article></section>
</Base>
